my $CODE = join("\n", map { "scroll line $_" } 1..40);

{
    desc => 'Ctrl-f scrolls viewport forward one full page',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/ctrl_f_page`

Tests that `Ctrl-f` scrolls the viewport forward (down) by one full page.
The buffer has 40 numbered lines so a full page scroll is clearly visible.

Keys: `Ctrl-f`

- **ctrl_f_page_initial.png**: Cursor at line 1 col 0 on "scroll line 1".
- **ctrl_f_page_after_ctrl_f.png**: Viewport scrolled forward one full page; cursor at bottom of new viewport.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-f');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_ctrl_f');
    },
}
